{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"for holy am I, YHWH, who sanctifies you\"</b> — He speaks together with the priests, just as He began, \"Speak to the priests,\" or \"I, YHWH, who sanctifies you\" — all of you, the priests and the people. And the reason is that since he offers the bread of your Elohim, he shall be holy to you, for through him I sanctify all of you and cause My Shekhinah to dwell in your sanctuary. And it is possible by way of truth that it refers back to the beginning of the verse, and this has already been explained."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:57:11.033742612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}